  *Academic notice.* This book is a doctoral-level academic text in psychology, psychotherapy, and the behavioural sciences. It is written for study, research, and professional education in marriage and family therapy. It is not clinical supervision, diagnosis, or treatment, and it does not by itself confer a doctoral or any other academic qualification. Doctoral standing depends on enrolment in a programme, supervised original research, and successful examination.

  *Professional notice.* Nothing in this book authorises or supports practice beyond the reader's training, competence, licensure, and lawful scope of practice, or practice that is contrary to the ethical codes and legal requirements of the jurisdiction concerned. Readers must obtain the current editions of the codes, statutes, and standards referred to in these pages; the law and professional regulation described are stated as understood at the date of writing (2026).

  *Research notice.* Studies, effect sizes, and findings are reported in summary form to support theoretical analysis. Readers who rely on a particular finding must consult the original publication, its methods, its sample, and any subsequent replication or critique.

  *Hypothetical material.* Cases, families, and scenarios marked as hypothetical are fictitious and are used exclusively for teaching and examination purposes. Any resemblance to actual persons or families is coincidental. Where case material derives from a published source, the source is cited.

  *Illustrations.* Diagrams and figures were prepared for this edition. Photographs marked "illustrative image (AI-generated)" were created for teaching purposes and do not depict any identifiable person, family, clinic, or agency.

